## 3. Mandatory Attribution

3.1 Every copy or Modification of the Program that is distributed must retain a clearly visible notice crediting the original author or original project as specified at the top of this document. This notice must include at least:

a) the name of the Program and the author/organization,
b) an indication that the work (or parts of it) is based on the named original,
c) a link or reference to the original source, where available.

3.2 Where a graphical user interface, "About" screen, documentation, or comparable customary location exists, the notice must be placed there. For pure libraries/code components, a notice in the documentation, credits, or associated metadata (e.g. license file, package description) is sufficient.

3.3 The notice may not be removed, obscured, or placed in a way that makes it practically undiscoverable to ordinary users.

3.4 You may not create the impression that a Modification originates entirely from you if substantial parts were taken from the original Program.

---

## 4. No-Sale Clause

4.1 The Program, unmodified copies of it, and Modifications of it may **not be sold** (see definition in Section 1.4).

4.2 This also applies if the Program or a Modification is distributed only as part of a larger, paid product or bundle — in that case, the portion attributable to the Program must remain free of charge, and the Program may not be advertised as a purchase incentive or as part of the purchase price.

4.3 Expressly permitted are:

a) voluntary donations to the creator of a Modification, where payment is not a prerequisite for receiving the Program,
b) offering paid support, customization, installation services, or consulting related to the Program,
c) charging fees for hosting, server operation, or infrastructure on which the Program runs, as long as the software itself is not sold but remains freely accessible,
d) advertising revenue in connection with providing the Program, provided the Program itself is not paid.

4.4 In case of doubt: if a mandatory payment is required to obtain a functional copy of the Program itself, this constitutes a Sale and is not permitted under this License.

