## How to Apply the PaperStream Permissive License to Your Own Program

Attach the following notice to the beginning of each source file:

```
[Program Name] — [Short description]
Copyright (C) [Year] [Author Name]
A [ORGANIZATION] project.

This program is licensed under the PaperStream Permissive License
(PSPL) v1.0. Use, modification, and distribution are freely permitted,
including in closed-source/proprietary software — provided that
attribution to the original author is retained and the program is
not sold. See LICENSE.md for the full terms.

A copy of the license should have been distributed with this program
(see LICENSE.md). If not, see [LINK TO YOUR REPO]/LICENSE.md.
```

Place this file as `LICENSE.md` in the root directory of each project. Fill in **[YEAR]**, **[AUTHOR NAME]**, **[PROJECT NAME]**, **[ORGANIZATION]**, and the **Description** individually for each project.

---

## Quick Comparison: PSL vs. PSPL

| | **PSL** (Copyleft) | **PSPL** (Permissive) |
|---|---|---|
| Source disclosure on distribution | Required | Not required |
| Network use (SaaS) must disclose source | Yes | No |
| Embedding in closed-source projects | No | Yes |
| Attribution to original author | Not explicitly required | **Required** |
| Selling the Program/Modifications | Not explicitly banned, but source must stay open regardless | **Explicitly banned** |
| Donations/support/hosting fees | Allowed | Allowed |
